  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/lucania_goodei_en/",
      "html": "<p>The Bluefin killifish originates from Florida and reaches a length of about 5 cm. In contrast to most other species of killifish this is a schooling species. The harmless mock fights of the males are marvelous to observe.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/lucania_goodei_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lucania goodei is found in hard water in the wild and prefers such conditions also in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/lucania_goodei_en/",
      "html": "<p>The Bluefin killifish spawns between plants and the eggs need about 14 days to hatch.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/lucania_goodei_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lucania: Latin, means \"the shining one\". goodei: dedication name.</p>"
    }
